From 599f7fa7862eff392d42072a4ac2ce8e51195fdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Elliott <aelliott@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:17:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [RISCV] Ensure Shadow Stack checks correct RA

This primarliy applies to the save-restore case, which was using
`__riscv_restore_<N>` incorrectly, entirely circumventing the software
shadow call stack.

This fix keeps the code size improvements of `__riscv_save_<N>` when
there is a shadow call stack, but it avoids the incorrect use of
`__riscv_restore_<N>`, instead emitting the correct sequence inline.

In the future, when there are better versions of `__riscv_save_<N>` and
`__riscv_restore_<N>` which support the shadow call stack variants (both
hardware and software), then we can revisit this approach and use the
correct pairs in all cases.
